    "deviations": [
      "--json-schema takes inline JSON only; a file path fails with 'is not valid JSON'. The caller reads the schema file and passes its text.",
      "The schema must not declare draft 2020-12 ($schema https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema is rejected: 'no schema with key or ref'); draft-07 works.",
      "env needs USER in addition to the 7.4 set: without it the cwork OAuth credential is not found in the Keychain ('Not logged in'). LOGNAME, TMPDIR or SHELL alone do not help."
    ],
    "verified": [
      "all flags exist in 2.1.295; --max-turns is accepted but hidden from -h",
      "--tools '' gives tools=[] in the init event; only the 6 broker tools (mcp__mac__*) are available",
      "--setting-sources '' is accepted",
      "structured_output appears in the result JSON even with --tools ''; it costs one extra model turn after finish()",
      "screencapture works from the broker (Screen Recording inherited from iTerm); window content visible"
    ],
    "phase5_notes": [
      "add --no-session-persistence: without it every run writes a ~370 KB transcript with base64 screenshots to ~/.claude-work/projects/<cwd-slug>/ (violates 'screenshots deleted after use'); with it only an empty memory/ dir is created",
      "startup: claude init is ~0.7 s without MCP and ~4.2 s with the stdio broker; the broker alone answers initialize in 0.6-1.5 s (mcp 2.x import ~1.2-1.5 s)",
      "time after finish() to process exit is 3.0-4.7 s (StructuredOutput turn + shutdown); the broker's finish record is authoritative, so the controller can return as soon as finish.json is written",
      "observe_screen varies 0.95-6.0 s (osascript System Events bounds + screencapture + sips)",
      "Calculator restores its last expression/result on launch, so a fresh launch can already show the target value; the runner leaves 49 after each run and checks the display independently"
    ]
  }
